-table {\n      width: 100%;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      font-size: 24px;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    .results-table col:first-child {\n      width: 45%;\n    }\n\n    .results-table col:nth-child(2),\n    .results-table col:nth-child(3) {\n      width: 27.5%;\n    }\n\n    .results-table thead th {\n      height: 75px;\n      padding: 13px 8px;\n      color: #fff;\n      background: #ef3532;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 24px;\n    }\n\n    .results-table tbody th,\n    .results-table tbody td {\n      height: 37px;\n      padding: 4px 8px;\n    }\n\n    .results-table tbody th {\n      color: #fff;\n      background: #42aec1;\n      font-style: italic;\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n\n    .results-table tbody tr:nth-child(odd) td {\n      background: #ebebeb;\n    }\n\n    .results-table tbody tr:nth-child(even) td {\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n\n    .table-notes {\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: flex-start;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      margin-top: 16px;\n      font-size: 24px;\n    }\n\n    .r-squared {\n      font-style: italic;\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n\n    .significance {\n      text-align: right;\n      font-size: 18px;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n      font-style: italic;\n    }\n\n    .conclusion {\n      padding: 22px 120px 70px;\n      min-height: 194px;\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n\n    .conclusion h2 {\n      margin-bottom: 25px;\n    }\n\n    .conclusion p {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 27px;\n      line-height: 1.4;\n    }\n\n    .references {\n      min-height: 237px;\n      padding: 67px 120px 55px;\n      color: #fff;\n      background: #030303;\n      font-size: 26px;\n      line-height: 1.5;\n    }\n\n    .references p {\n      margin: 0;\n    }\n\n    .references strong {\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 1728px) {\n      body {\n        display: block;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n      }\n    }\n\n    @media print {\n      html,\n      body {\n        width: 1728px;\n        background: #fff;\n      }\n\n      .poster {\n        width: 1728px;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"poster\">\n    <header class=\"hero\">\n      <div class=\"hero-photo placeholder\">[Photo: person using a mobile device, red overlay]</div>\n      <div class=\"hero-copy\">\n        <h1>The sales effect of “Free App of the Day”<br>on Amazon Appstore: An empirical study</h1>\n        <div class=\"authors\">Hong Chen, Kevin Lachaud, Wenqi Zhou</div>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <section class=\"introduction-zone\">\n      <div class=\"phone-photo placeholder\" aria-label=\"Photo of a hand using a smartphone\">\n        [Photo: hand using a smartphone]\n        <div class=\"phone\"></div>\n        <div class=\"hand-finger\"></div>\n        <div class=\"hand-palm\"></div>\n        <div class=\"wrist\"></div>\n        <div class=\"watch-band\"></div>\n        <div class=\"watch-face\"></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Introduction</h2>\n        <p>\n          Apps, as an abbreviation of mobile applications, are software products for mobile platforms\n          (Tang, 2016). They are designed to perform certain tasks on mobile devices (Islam, Islam, &amp;\n          Mazumder, 2010). This product category has grown to become a gigantic differentiated market\n          with over 3.48 million apps on Google Play, an app marketplace, and the recent projection of\n          over 935-billion-dollar revenue in 2023 (Statista Research, 2021a, Statista Research, 2021b).\n        </p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"objective\">\n        <h2>Objective</h2>\n        <p>This work studies the adverse effect of “Free App of the Day” at Amazon Appstore.</p>\n      </section>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"content-zone\">\n      <div class=\"columns\">\n        <section class=\"methodology\">\n          <h2>Methodology</h2>\n          <ol class=\"method-list\">\n            <li>\n              <strong>1. Literature review</strong>\n              <div class=\"sub-list\">\n                a. Digital free sampling<br>\n                b. eWOM\n              </div>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong>2. Hypotheses</strong>\n              <div class=\"hypothesis\">\n                a. H1 - Online user decisions to adopt apps are discouraged by the price rebound after the zero-price\n                offering of FAD ends. The sharper price rebound leads to a greater decrease in app adoptions.\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"hypothesis\">\n                b. H2 - Conditional on the total volume of eWOM, organic reviews are more influential to online user\n                decisions of adopting apps than promotion-induced reviews after the FAD promotion ends.\n              </div>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong>3. Data</strong>\n              <div class=\"sub-list\">\n                a. Context and data collection<br>\n                b. Key variables\n              </div>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong>4. Empirical analysis</strong>\n              <div class=\"sub-list\">\n                a. Exploratory analysis<br>\n                b. Regression model and results\n              </div>\n            </li>\n          </ol>\n        </section>\n\n        <div class=\"divider\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n\n        <section class=\"results\">\n          <h2>Results</h2>\n          <p>\n            We notice that a few apps were off the direct spotlight post-promotion; however, they still offer zero price for\n            another one or two days.<br>\n            Specifically, an increase in SkewDaily indicates a more right skewed distribution of daily number of reviews\n            during the post-promotion period.\n          </p>\n\n          <table class=\"results-table\">\n            <colgroup>\n              <col>\n              <col>\n              <col>\n            </colgroup>\n            <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th>Empty Cell</th>\n                <th>Mean</th>\n                <th>S.D.</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr>\n                <th>PriceRebound<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>−0.40***</td>\n                <td>0.06</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>SkewDaily<sub>i</sub></th>\n                <td>−0.19*</td>\n                <td>0.11</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>KurtDdaily<sub>i</sub></th>\n                <td>−0.09**</td>\n                <td>0.05</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>Ln(NumReviews<sub>i,t</sub>)</th>\n                <td>0.59***</td>\n                <td>0.08</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>AverageRating<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>2.06***</td>\n                <td>0.40</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>VarianceRating<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>1.17***</td>\n                <td>0.30</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>Day<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>−0.11*</td>\n                <td>0.03</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>Age<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>−0.0004***</td>\n                <td>0.0002</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th>AppSize<sub>i,t</sub></th>\n                <td>0.01***</td>\n                <td>0.002</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n\n          <div class=\"table-notes\">\n            <div class=\"r-squared\">R2 = 0.45</div>\n            <div class=\"significance\">\n              * p &lt; 0.1.<br>\n              **p &lt; 0.05.<br>\n              ***p &lt; 0.01.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"conclusion\">\n      <h2>Conclusion</h2>\n      <p>We conclude that these promotion-induced reviews are less influential than organic reviews.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <footer class=\"references\">\n      <p>\n        <strong>References:</strong> Chen, H., Lachaud, K. and Zhou, W., 2022. The sales effect of “Free App of the Day” on Amazon Appstore:<br>\n        An empirical study. Digital Business, 2(2), p.100020.\n      </p>\n    </footer>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
